### Requests to poke the running app (make up). Works with the VS Code REST
### Client or JetBrains HTTP Client; the curl equivalents are in comments.
@base = http://localhost:8080

### Register a venue            curl -i -X POST $base/venues -d '{...}'
# @name register
POST {{base}}/venues
Content-Type: application/json

{"name": "Coliseu dos Recreios", "street": "Rua Portas de Santo Antão 96", "city": "Lisboa", "country": "PT"}

### Lay it out: a seated section…
@venue = {{register.response.body.id}}
POST {{base}}/venues/{{venue}}/sections
Content-Type: application/json

{"code": "ORCH", "name": "Orchestra", "kind": "seated", "rows": [{"label": "A", "seats": 10}, {"label": "B", "seats": 12}]}

### …and a standing one
POST {{base}}/venues/{{venue}}/sections
Content-Type: application/json

{"code": "FLOOR", "name": "Floor", "kind": "ga", "capacity": 500}

### Activate it (VEN-5)
POST {{base}}/venues/{{venue}}/activation

### Read it back: status active, capacity 522
GET {{base}}/venues/{{venue}}

### List active venues
GET {{base}}/venues?status=active

### Retire it (VEN-6)
POST {{base}}/venues/{{venue}}/retirement
